why: run 7 wrote "The run hash derives from these names, so the dataset files a renamed member's results under a fresh history" on an enum whose members' values name the ledger's format cells; a reviewer read it on 2026-09-22 and said the second part was garbage and hard to follow, and code review found it false: the cell name is the member's value, so renaming a member that keeps its value changes nothing, and "a rename" reads either way; the fact is that the results dataset keys on the member's value, and the tie names the enum and what a changed value does
labelled: 2026-09-22
--- code
export enum PostingFormat {
  Accrual = 'accrual',
  Deferred = 'deferred',
  Reversal = 'reversal',
}
--- facts
The results dataset keys each stored row on a member's value, and no row is found again under a value that changed.

# claimed at this site by an earlier run:
The run hash derives from these names, so the dataset files a renamed member's results under a fresh history.
